# MCP tool credentials (for huawei-auto-pal's supplementary data sources)
# Copy this file to .env (in the same directory) and fill in your real values.
# .env is gitignored — never commit real tokens. Verify with:
#   git check-ignore .env && git ls-files .env   # should print the path, then nothing

# --- CodeHub — Huawei internal Git platform (optional) ---
# Used by skill-forge to read MR reviews and issues from Huawei internal repos.
# Get a token from CodeHub → Settings → Access Tokens (https://codehub-g.huawei.com/).
# CODEHUB_HOST: codehub-g.huawei.com is reachable from most networks (recommended);
#   codehub-y.huawei.com may be unreachable on some segments.
# Confirm reachability:
#   NO_PROXY=*.huawei.com curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://codehub-g.huawei.com/
CODEHUB_TOKEN=your_codehub_personal_access_token_here
CODEHUB_HOST=https://codehub-g.huawei.com/

# --- GitHub — external Git platform (DISABLED) ---
# The GitHub wrapper (mcp-tools/github/github_mcp.py) uses ssl.CERT_NONE, which
# disables TLS verification. Until that is independently fixed and validated,
# huawei-auto-pal does NOT call the GitHub MCP tool and does NOT ask you to
# create a token. Do not set GITHUB_TOKEN.
# GitHub 封装存在 TLS 安全问题，已禁用，暂无需配置。
#GITHUB_TOKEN=your_github_personal_access_token_here

# --- CloudDevOps Wiki — Huawei internal wiki (optional) ---
# Read operations (search, fetch content) need NO token.
# User-level queries and write operations need WIKI_X_AUTH_TOKEN.
# Get it from the CloudDevOps platform (browser cookie or settings page).
#WIKI_X_AUTH_TOKEN=your_wiki_x_auth_token_here
